Honey App database migrations managed by Alembic.
Run alembic upgrade head after modifying versions under migrations/versions.

Irreversible migrations (NOC-029): if a migration's downgrade() cannot
actually restore data that upgrade() deletes or mutates (e.g. dropping a
column or table that already held real rows), mark it explicitly so
scripts/upgrade.py's pre-flight check can warn and abort before an
automated upgrade applies it, instead of silently running a downgrade()
that "succeeds" but has already lost data:

    irreversible = True
    irreversible_reason = "drops the X column; its data cannot be recovered by downgrade()"

Leave both unset (the default) when downgrade() genuinely restores the
prior schema/data losslessly -- true for every migration in this repo
today.
